; bfsodium HMAC_SHA_512 : RFC 2104 keyed hashing  with SHA_512
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The hash is sha512/hashcore  PASTED  and entered up to
; three times: once for a key longer than a block  once inside and once out;
;
; As in sha512/hashcore  a run of ONE repeated token is a repetition rather
; than a decision and is written as such; every offset  every branch and both
; sixteen word pads below were worked out from the map and written down;
;
; INTERFACE entry=517 exit=520 footprint=0:2671
; IO  in:  klen{2} LE  mplen{2} LE  mslen{2} LE  kbuf{256}  mbuf{256}
;          then mslen bytes from the wire
;     out: mac{64}  big endian
;
; The message is mplen bytes from mbuf followed by mslen bytes off the wire;
; either count may be nought; That is hashcore's own two source shape passed
; straight through  because HKDF builds its messages in memory and a caller
; hashing something that arrives on the wire should not have to buffer it;
;
; Only the first klen bytes of kbuf and the first mplen of mbuf are looked at
; and the rest MUST be nought; padding the key to a block leans on it;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x001  klen{2}  u16 LE  the key's length
;   @0x002:0x003  mplen{2} u16 LE  message bytes in mbuf; at most 128
;   @0x004:0x005  mslen{2} u16 LE  message bytes on the wire
;   @0x006:0x105  kbuf{256} u8     the key  as given
;   @0x106:0x205  mbuf{256} u8     the message prefix  as given
;   @0x208:0x94b  sha512/hashcore's frame  pasted at @0x208; footprint 0:1859
;   @0x950:0x9cf  kpad{128} u8     the key padded to a block  kept for both pads
;   @0x9d0:0xa0f  inner{64} u8     the inner digest  as a byte string
;   @0xa10:0xa17  the long key flag  the hundred and twenty eight step counter
;                          and the cells the length comparison is made through
;   @0xa1c:0xa41  the exclusive or frame; xor64 footprint 0:37 at @0xa1c
;   @0xa48:0xa63  the adder frame; add64 footprint 0:27 at @0xa48
;   @0xa68:0xa6f  tmp{8}   hands a word back after it has been copied
;
; HMAC is  H( (K xor opad) then H( (K xor ipad) then message ) )  where K is the
; key padded to a block with noughts  or the key's own hash if it was longer
; than one; ipad is the byte 0x36 a hundred and twenty eight times and opad is
; 0x5c;
;
; A DIGEST IS A BYTE STRING AND H IS WORDS; hashcore leaves its answer in H as
; eight little endian words  and the digest the standard defines is those words
; written most significant byte first; the emit does that reversal on the way
; out  and so must every path that feeds a digest back IN as message bytes:
; the inner digest here  and the hash of an over long key; Getting it wrong
; costs a mac that is right in every part except the order of eight bytes at a
; time; Both reversals walk their source LEFT while the destination walks
; RIGHT  so one set of distances shrinks by two a step and the other grows;
;
; The key is compared against a block by a hundred and twenty eight borrowing
; decrements of a copy rather than by a general comparison; the count is small
; the code is one loop  and a general byte comparison in brainfuck is neither
; of those things;
;
; THE SAME SHAPE AS sha256/hmac  section for section; The block is twice as
; long so the pads run sixteen words rather than eight  the digest is sixty
; four bytes  and the message prefix a caller may hand in is a hundred and
; twenty eight rather than a hundred and ninety two  since the pad block now
; takes half of hashcore's prefix buffer; The eight flag cells sit at the same
; offsets from their own base as they do there  so the whole length comparison
; is that file's code with four numbers changed;

; read the three counts  the key and the message prefix
,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
